### Run auth-hiring-setup + check-mvp5-messaging, then:
### TEST_SESSION=.local/hiring-session.json python3 scripts/http-env.py
### Choose local. Tokens exist only in the ignored private environment. Always sync after switching accounts.
@base = http://localhost:8080

### Obtain conservative snapshot boundary before opening each independent stream.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/conversations/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

> {% client.global.set("messaging_cursor", response.body.cursor); %}

### Copy cursor from sync or last event. Heartbeats do not advance it.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/conversations/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Last-Event-ID: {{messaging_cursor}}
Accept: text/event-stream

### Notification snapshot/count and independent stream cursor
GET {{base}}/api/v1/notifications/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

> {% client.global.set("notification_cursor", response.body.cursor); %}

### 410 means re-synchronize; 401 means refresh via PKCE before reconnect.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/notifications/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Last-Event-ID: {{notification_cursor}}
Accept: text/event-stream

### My private preferences; idempotent, does not mark read.
PATCH {{base}}/api/v1/conversations/{{conversation_id}}/preferences
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"muted":true,"archived":true}

### Archived conversations remain readable; next new message unarchives participants.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/conversations?archived=true&size=50
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### Explicit monotonic read position; syncs only my devices.
PUT {{base}}/api/v1/conversations/{{conversation_id}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"messageId":"{{message_id}}"}

### B sends through REST; both A devices receive only an invalidation.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/conversations/{{conversation_id}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"clientMessageId":"{{$uuid}}","body":"Local live update verification"}

> {% client.global.set("message_id", response.body.id); %}

### Select one of my durable notifications; target content still requires its own authorized API.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/notifications?size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

> {% if (response.body.length) client.global.set("notification_id", response.body[0].id); %}

### Explicit notification read; does not depend on socket delivery.
PUT {{base}}/api/v1/notifications/{{notification_id}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

